# Level one

The first browse level introduces broad topics and routes to their subtopics. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/frontend-templates/mainstream-browse/level-one/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

Use a first level only when the documentation or household help collection is large enough to need it. Choose broad, familiar subjects and a one-sentence description when names alone are ambiguous. A smaller setup should keep its direct task links visible.

## Structure and behaviour

A topic page contains a clear heading, concise introduction and a plain list of subtopics. Curated high-priority links may appear first when their importance is evidenced; do not label them “Most viewed” without actual appropriate evidence. Keep topic links and immediate device actions separate.

## Home Assistant boundary

The government’s popularity ranking is not a household requirement. This reference does not collect analytics or change native HA areas. A first-level page must not become an extra compulsory click before every common task.

